# Curated artefact — Phase 4, QHV twin leg, Windows half.
# qemu: 11.0.50 (v11.0.0-12631-g54e84cdc7a, fork build); devices: virtio-blk only
# (no rng: ~19 s of entropy-timeout artefact per run); disk: no -snapshot.
# Superseded as the Windows baseline by windows-qhv-tcg-rng-slot3-boot-times-n5.txt;
# kept as the record of the first instrumented series. "Identical invocation"
# below is true of the argument list only — see docs/digital-twin-design.md §1a.
# 2026-09-11: the chain continues: rng-slot3 -> rng-snapshot-segments -> the q111 release-aligned
# pair (windows- and orin-qhv-tcg-q111-rng-snapshot-segments-boot-times-n5.txt); all A3 history.
#
# Run 1 of a 5-run timed series produced by:
#     scripts\launch-qhv-tcg.ps1 -Runs 5 -StopOnGuestBanner -CaptureSeconds 280
#
# QEMU invocation (identical on both twin hosts by design — the Orin half is
# scripts/orin/launch-qhv-on-orin-tcg.sh):
#     qemu-system-aarch64 -machine virt,virtualization=on,gic-version=3 \
#       -cpu max -accel tcg -smp 2 -m 2G \
#       -drive file=disk-qemu,if=none,id=drv0,format=raw \
#       -device virtio-blk-device,drive=drv0 -kernel ifs.bin \
#       -serial file:<log> -display none -no-reboot
#
# TCG, and NOT for the usual reason: QHV needs EL2 for its guest, i.e. nested
# virtualisation, which ARM KVM does not provide on A78AE. TCG here is a hard
# architectural requirement on both hosts, not the GICv3/KVM_EXIT_ARM_NISV
# blockage that forces TCG on the separate qnx-safety-vm leg. Do not conflate
# the two when quoting these numbers.
#
# WHAT TO LOOK FOR — three markers, in this order. Note that the QHV *host*
# prints NO banner of its own; an earlier curation note on
# qhv-tcg-host-and-guest-boot.log claimed it did, and that was wrong (see
# docs/findings.md, 2026-09-08). Only the guest has a banner.
#
#   1. "=== AUTO-START QNX GUEST UNDER QVM"   host reached post_start
#   2. "=== launching qvm @g2.conf"           hypervisor invoked
#   3. "QNX qnx-guest ... ARMv8_Foundation_Model"
#                                             guest up across the EL2/EL1 boundary
#
# Lines 1-26 of the body are the QHV host booting; the host's post_start then
# starts the guest under qvm, and the rc sequence repeats for the guest.
#
# The measured value is wall-clock launch -> marker 3. The host's
# post_start.custom holds a hard-coded "sleep 90" boot-grace, but the guest
# banner lands at ~49 s, inside that sleep, so it does not pad the number.
#
# The io-sock / vtnet0 / entropy errors below are known and expected on this
# leg: it does no host networking at all (no br0, no tap). See
# docs/findings.md's 2026-07-28 entry on the Orin virtio-rng ordering issue for
# the related-but-separate networking story on the other leg.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

